WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.920
Miyazaki just did a bunch of interviews, and
we learned a lot of really significant things.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.940
For example..see this weapon art?

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:14.210
Turns out, it's not specific to this weapon..instead,
you can mix and match weapon arts to multiple

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:15.210
weapons.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.320
See this pot boy?

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.720
You might be able to capture enemies like
this, and summon them as spirit helpers that

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.199
fight alongside you.

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:29.029
Bosses can supposedly be tackled in any order..

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:32.349
The story is fascinating..and

00:00:32.349 --> 00:00:37.280
..multiplayer is meant to be more convenient
than ever before.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:42.410
Elden Ring news has only just begun..so please
subscribe, and keep up with it all.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:47.320
For the purposes of this video though, I've
split the information into four categories.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.790
Gameplay, the Open World, Multiplayer, and
Story.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.680
First up, Gameplay.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.940
Specifically, combat.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.829
Elden Ring will see the return of the stamina
bar - though Miyazaki notes that he feels

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:01.190
it has less influence on the player overall.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:08.109
If I had to speculate, perhaps it feels more
akin to Bloodborne, where stamina stops you

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:13.799
spamming actions up to a certain point, but
still allows for faster paced gameplay.

00:01:13.799 --> 00:01:20.139
They've obviously learned a lot from working
on Sekiro..and like Sekiro, Elden Ring also

00:01:20.139 --> 00:01:22.329
has an implementation of stealth.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:27.009
You can crouch to sneak up on enemies, bypass
certain areas, or simply assess situations

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:28.909
while hiding in long grass.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:35.249
Additionally, when night falls, your stealth
is enhanced..but your visibility is decreased,

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:39.109
and some scary enemies will only appear at
night, as well.

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:44.029
Elden Ring now also has a jump button, allowing
you to avoid sweeping attacks, and perform

00:01:44.029 --> 00:01:46.959
jump attacks that differ based on the weapon
you wield.

00:01:46.959 --> 00:01:53.020
Furthermore, fall damage has been greatly
reduced to encourage your vertical exploration.

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.929
And unlike any From game before it, Elden
Ring has horseback combat - though Miyazaki

00:01:56.929 --> 00:02:01.669
stresses that most battles will still be done
on foot, except for certain fights where you

00:02:01.669 --> 00:02:04.149
might need the extra mobility.

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:11.349
But the newest, most fascinating addition
to Elden Ring's gameplay..are "summonable

00:02:11.349 --> 00:02:12.769
spirits".

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:18.909
As seen briefly in the trailer, these are
enemy-based spirits that fight alongside you..fulfilling

00:02:18.909 --> 00:02:24.680
certain roles, like tanking for you, attacking
from range, or assisting you in melee.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:28.739
They're able to be levelled up, and maybe
even customised.

00:02:28.739 --> 00:02:34.430
Now, they can't be summoned everywhere..but
they are something you're supposed to consider

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:40.040
as a part of your build, similar to how you
pick a weapon.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.870
And like weapons..who you choose to summon
will come down to personal taste.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:50.340
Miyazaki himself says players might often
enjoy a certain enemy tagging along with them,

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.370
even if they're not of much use in combat.

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.530
Pot boy, I choose you!

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:59.170
It's funny..ever since I saw Father Owl summon
a bird that defends him, I thought this would

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:03.310
make a good addition to the game..and it's
crazy that it's actually a thing now.

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:07.670
In fact, you literally see a character summon
a bird here.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:14.040
Spirits having specific roles and unique animations
is so, so much better than another human NPC

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.859
following you around, like in Dark souls.

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:24.150
Overall though, Elden Ring is probably closest
to Dark Souls in terms of gameplay and combat.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:29.530
This is what I expected - but what I didn't
expect was how deep they're going with build

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:31.000
customisation.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:37.980
Because in addition to magic, weapons, armour,
and spirit summons..you also have "skills".

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:43.340
So in Dark Souls, every weapon had a different
weapon art, special attacks that could be

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.650
activated with L2.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.959
Sekiro also had combat arts, which you could
equip to your character, and perform by holding

00:03:50.959 --> 00:03:56.170
L1 and pressing R1.

00:03:56.170 --> 00:04:02.700
Now, in Elden Ring..we have "skills", which
are kind of a combination of Weapon Arts,

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.670
and Combat Arts.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:11.459
There are around a hundred skills in total,
and they can be freely assigned to a large

00:04:11.459 --> 00:04:13.120
variety of weapons.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.639
So you see this jump back slash the character
is doing with this curved sword?

00:04:18.639 --> 00:04:23.361
If you liked the skill, but not the weapon..you
could assign this skill to a different weapon.

00:04:23.361 --> 00:04:24.361
If you're about to face a boss that would
be weak to a certain weapon art, perhaps you

00:04:24.361 --> 00:04:25.361
can even apply that weapon art on the fly.

00:04:25.361 --> 00:04:30.300
This is an insane amount of build variety,
pvp players are going to love this, and it

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.720
will help fill the open world with discoverable
abilities.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:40.240
The open world is also filled with crafting
materials, which you can search for to create

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.240
the items you need most.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:48.050
A lot of these, says Miyazaki, will be healing
items, which will be necessary since you might

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:53.630
be fighting for a longer time between checkpoints,
than in previous games.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:59.669
Of course, experience in-game can also be
used to level up your character.

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:06.669
So between skills, spirit summons, weapons,
magic, armour, consumables and crafting materials..you'll

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:12.740
have a ton of tools at your disposal to take
on the world.

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:18.990
This will almost certainly affect the difficulty
of the game, specifically its skill floor.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:23.669
Something like Sekiro, for example, has a
very high skill floor.

00:05:23.669 --> 00:05:29.349
In order to progress, you literally have to
have the mechanical skill to overcome certain

00:05:29.349 --> 00:05:35.039
fights- you can't rely on levelling up your
character, or using tools that the boss is

00:05:35.039 --> 00:05:36.170
weak to.

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:41.650
Elden Ring, on the other hand, will offer
ways in-game to overcome difficulty..just

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.650
like Dark Souls did.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.479
This isn't a bad thing - it just means that
if you're lacking a bit of mechanical skill,

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:54.800
difficulty can also be overcome with with
preparation, co-operation, and exploration.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.050
While exploring the massive world, you'll
also have access to a World Map, which you

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:04.669
can consult to see where you are, where you've
been, and where you've yet to go.

00:06:04.669 --> 00:06:10.190
This map will work in the open world, but
not in the smaller spaces of each map.

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:16.580
These "legacy" dungeons are more akin to what
we're used to in Dark Souls, and each open

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:23.539
world will have its own main dungeon, as well
as catacombs, camps, and fortresses interspersed

00:06:23.539 --> 00:06:25.740
throughout the map.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:32.569
There are six Open Worlds that we'll be exploring,
each the domain of "demigod" characters that

00:06:32.569 --> 00:06:36.349
we'll discuss in another video.

00:06:36.349 --> 00:06:42.570
These areas are called the "Lands Between",
and they're arranged in such a way that there

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:47.690
is a logical progression to them, though you
don't have to follow it.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:52.669
In fact, you can skip more than half the game's
bosses if you want to.

00:06:52.669 --> 00:06:58.020
In that sense, it sounds a lot like Breath
of the Wild, where the main path is quite

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:02.520
clear, but side paths are tempting to explore.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:07.439
According to Miyazaki, none of these side
paths, or side quests will appear on your

00:07:07.439 --> 00:07:08.439
map.

00:07:08.439 --> 00:07:13.280
Instead, it's up to the player to mark these
things themselves manually, which I think

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.280
is fantastic for immersion.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:20.250
A little later in the game, the player will
be able to access a hub area, where you can

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.580
branch out into the six main areas of the
Lands Between.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:30.169
On top of this, fast travel is also present,
though From Software encourage users to enjoy

00:07:30.169 --> 00:07:34.280
the exploration and uncover the map for themselves.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:40.289
Like in all open world games, the more you
discover, the more powerful your character

00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:46.979
becomes..and I'm sure the difficulty of a
From Software will be a great motivator for

00:07:46.979 --> 00:08:07.580
exploration.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:15.080
Another motivator for exploration are meetings
with plot characters, who add drama to the

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:21.039
journey, twists to the narrative, and influence
the endings.

00:08:21.039 --> 00:08:28.470
According to Miyazaki, the NPCs you meet will
have a big impact on your worldview, and reveal

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.110
how they see the world.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:35.730
In fact, he calls them "protagonists", and
says they're an "extremely important" part

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:41.460
of Elden Ring, which is certainly more than
he's said about NPCs in past games.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:49.840
For all these NPC's however, there will be
no bustling towns, or villages, in Elden Ring.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:59.060
This isn't their specialty, he says, so they've
chosen to focus on other things.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:06.190
The usual story presentation methods through
item descriptions and dialogue are to be expected,

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:10.880
though the team says they're also leveraging
what they've learned from Sekiro and will

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:16.730
be better able to present the surface plot
through dialogue and cutscenes.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:22.790
What is different this time, is how the story
of this game came to be written.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:28.850
In the past, Miyazaki says, he would set a
game system and then write a story that matches

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:32.470
that - but this time, it was the opposite.

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:37.310
George Martin wrote the foundations of the
story - he came up with the mythos of the

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:43.980
world..including the Tarnished and the 6 demigods..and
THEN the team applied gameplay systems to

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:45.300
suit that.

00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:51.050
They said that they expected to have to leave
out parts of the mythos to suit the game systems,

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:57.310
but that it ended up not being like that,
and that the collaboration was a very fruitful

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:58.310
one.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.650
We actually already know quite a bit about
the lore of the game, and it's really helped

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:05.370
to contextualise a lot of the stuff in the
original trailer.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.280
Please, stay tuned for that in my next video.

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:09.320
Speaking of collaboration, the developers
are aiming to make it easier to co-op.

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:14.680
Firstly, resources like humanity and embers
previously needed for co-op have been reduced,

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.980
or removed.

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:20.920
Secondly, special locations exist in the world
where players can leave their signs to see

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:22.900
who is currently available.

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:29.920
Lastly, once you're sharing a world, it seems
interface elements will be added to provide

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.110
information about other players in the world.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:39.120
To enhance the connection you have to those
around you, "Groups" are being added to the

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:40.120
game.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:46.920
Once you join a group, you'll be able to single
out the phantoms, bloodstains, and messages

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:51.900
from others in your group, allowing you to
connect on a more relatable level.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:57.200
For example, I'll probably be able to set
the password "Vaati", and you guys will be

00:10:57.200 --> 00:11:03.840
able to see and connect with what everyone
in our community is doing.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:07.710
On top of this, the game will also have covenants,
which often add flavour to the multiplayer.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:13.540
So this would be something like the Aldritch
Faithful from Dark Souls 3, for example, where

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:17.950
you role-play as a defender of Aldritch.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:25.160
PvP is of course confirmed, even in the massive
open field, which is a nice surprise.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:32.050
That said, Miyazaki says that you won't be
able to use your horse in the open field..which..confuses

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.050
me.

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:38.930
I can see how PvP might be awkward on horseback..but
I wonder how they're going to stop two fighting

00:11:58.459 --> 00:12:05.779
so necessary?

